<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <!-- The id below is derived from the stem passed to `dotnet new bbpkg -n <Stem>`; the assembly
         name stays the bare stem, which is the convention across these repos. -->
    <PackageId>Bennewitz.Ninja.AssemblyQuality</PackageId>
    <AssemblyName>AssemblyQuality</AssemblyName>
    <Description>Static analysis rules for the shape a .NET assembly ships: cancellation contracts, implementation types leaking through the public surface, layering the reference list can prove, and namespace segments that shadow a dependency's root and fail with CS0234 at the use site. Rules report findings and an inspected count rather than asserting, so a consumer picks the runner and the severity. The assembly-shaped companion to Bennewitz.Ninja.XamlQuality.</Description>
    <PackageTags>static-analysis;reflection;public-api;api-surface;architecture;layering;cancellation;namespaces;quality;testing</PackageTags>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <!-- Runs the trim, AOT and single-file analyzers; TreatWarningsAsErrors makes them binding.
         The library is NOT trim-safe and cannot be: every reflection entry point says so with
         [RequiresUnreferencedCode] instead, and this is what keeps a new one from going unmarked. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
